+| 9e21ed682 | 2026-11-26 | Face takes a start point and an exit point: the raster starts at the corner nearest the start point, and the last row ends on the side nearest the exit point or the cut is refused by name (#3326). 2D Contour: a start or exit point under a Z-rotated work offset is now read in the setup's frame; before, the cut entered and left on the wrong wall (#3326, PR #3997) | 0.27.0 |
+| 034e91b8b | 2026-11-25 | Sinker Burn and Sinker Side Burn take a start point and an exit point: the angle at which the orbit starts and ends, and the end of the side move where the electrode plunges and retracts. An impossible point is refused by name (#3333, PR #3980) | 0.27.0 |
+| 83d52ef6a | 2026-11-25 | Wire Contour: a tangent arc lead-in and lead-out (`lead_arc_radius`, mm) for a selected DXF profile, next to the straight lead; a lead that does not fit is refused by name (#3937, #3991, PR #4002) | 0.27.0 |
+| 6f4131bd9 | 2026-11-25 | Drill, Bore and Thread (mill) take a start point and an exit point as the hole order: the picked hole is cut first or last, and a point that is on no hole is refused by name (#3328, PR #3970) | 0.27.0 |
+| 1327aef22 | 2026-11-25 | MCP `list_operation_types` names every field that a kind accepts: optional fields are marked `optional`, enum fields list their `values`, and object fields show their `shape` (#3449, PR #4033) | 0.27.0 |
+| 3bb6647f6 | 2026-11-25 | Wire EDM: a Wire Contour of a meshed model posts its circles and fillets as true G2 / G3 arcs (read back from the facets within the model chord tolerance), not as G01 chords (#3215, PR #4019) | 0.27.0 |
+| 612b47e69 | 2026-11-25 | `camcraft-cli --ui` uses a window's link file only while that window holds its lock. A stale file of a crashed window is removed and never dialed, and a link file without that proof is skipped with the reason (#3995, PR #4020) | 0.27.0 |
+| a3acba407 | 2026-11-25 | The 5-Axis Contour takes a start point and an exit point: each closed waterline ring starts at its point nearest the start pick and, after its lap, leaves at its point nearest the exit pick; a pick that cannot be held is refused by name (#3330, PR #4006) | 0.27.0 |
+| 49bfcaea8 | 2026-11-25 | The Rotary Flow band's stated rotation axis and radial retract are editable in the operation panel, and its icon renders in the ribbon (#2827, PR #4007) | 0.27.0 |
+| cd727156d | 2026-11-25 | Rotary Flow: the field eye now cuts the kind (parity proved against the radial law), and on a spindle C with stated travel the band unwinds by whole turns at its radial retract links instead of refusing (#2828, PR #4005) | 0.27.0 |
+| 138a592a1 | 2026-11-25 | `camcraft-cli --skill <folder\|claude\|copilot> install` writes an AI agent skill for the CLI (lanes, exit codes, examples and the full help text). It refuses to replace an existing file without `--force` (#3751, PR #4011) | 0.27.0 |
+| 9caa0d572 | 2026-11-25 | Turning: Facing, Profile Rough and Profile Finish take a start point and an exit point in the lathe (Z, X) plane; a point that the laws cannot hold is refused by name (#3331, PR #3981) | 0.27.0 |
+| 7ada53b51 | 2026-11-25 | Simulate: the stock playback cuts operations that have linear moves only (ball or flat end mill) with the GPU kernel on the window's graphics device, when it is a hardware adapter; the CPU playback runs in each other case (#2629, #3336, PR #4001) | 0.27.0 |
+| baad348f1 | 2026-11-25 | Agie-only controls (the nominal inspection section, the inspection export action and the open-cut clamp statements) now show only for a setup on the Agie machine or with the native Agie post (#3996, PR #4003) | 0.27.0 |
+| 52ba36ded | 2026-11-25 | A Slot takes a start point and an exit point: the pass starts at the slot end nearest the start point and stops at the end nearest the exit point, or the operation is refused by name (#3325, PR #3978) | 0.27.0 |
+| 6bcbbeb79 | 2026-11-25 | The verifier shares prismatic model sections for geometric queries and skips distant wall probes. Collision reach checks keep the exact samples from every cut plane (#3831, PR #3977) | 0.27.0 |
+| b533a8c89 | 2026-11-25 | Rotary Flow, a multiaxis flow-line operation over picked guide chains, is wired into the app: parameters, project file (v82), generation, verify, the editor and its glyph (#2826, PR #3999) | 0.27.0 |
+| b699135e8 | 2026-11-25 | The tool Properties page is now a summary with an "Edit in tool library" button. The holder pick moved from the tool shape window to the tool library window, and the window's Tool tab has a folded Body section (holder cylinder, body import and placement, pieces) (#3930, PR #3994) | 0.27.0 |
+| 73f9803d4 | 2026-11-25 | DXF import reads SPLINE and ELLIPSE entities as tangent arcs within 1 µm, so a drawing with a spline or an ellipse no longer stops the import and its curves can feed a wire contour; INSERT and POINT entities are skipped and counted instead of stopping the import (#1865, #3937, PR #3958) | 0.27.0 |
+| d80dc6944 | 2026-11-25 | Wire EDM: two tangent arcs of a drawn profile now join arc to arc; the program has no `G1` block with no motion between them (#3937, #3959, PR #3988) | 0.27.0 |
+| 0bb9bda5a | 2026-11-25 | The 3D tool preview shows helical flutes on end, ball and bull nose mills, drills and chamfer mills (the flute count and the helix angle; display only), with a Flutes toggle (#3908, PR #3989) | 0.27.0 |
+| f287a370c | 2026-11-25 | Rotary Contour, Rotary Parallel and Rotary Offset read a stated rotation axis first (the operation's own direction, else the machine's stated rotary line through the work offset origin), judged against the model's faces - a part on the stated line cuts the fitted path unchanged, a part whose faces disagree refuses by name (the 4-axis case named), and nothing stated keeps the fitted axis (v81 project files - a breaking project-format change) (#2772, PR #3674) | 0.27.0 |
+| 10ea81a2a | 2026-11-24 | Wire Contour takes an exit point: an open run ends at the end nearest the pick, and a closed profile is left at the pick after its full lap; a pick the wire cannot hold is refused by name (#3332, PR #3957) | 0.27.0 |
+| 97a676e5c | 2026-11-24 | A 2D Chamfer can select a tip offset and cut through that cone band while preserving the authored chamfer width (#3153, PR #3251) | 0.27.0 |
+| 0e305577b | 2026-11-24 | UI link: verify token proof from window and bound line reads (#3874, PR #3883) | 0.27.0 |
+| 72a38bea2 | 2026-11-24 | Tests: the last unguarded GPU tests of the UI `egui_app` and lib binaries now run one at a time (#3379, PR #3972) | 0.27.0 |
